2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': 'e851a0a4-0090-44cd-8882-efca5055781d', '_id': 'Documents/e851a0a4-0090-44cd-8882-efca5055781d', '_rev': '_envYS8S--A', 'createDate': '2022-08-14T12:35:41.669Z', 'data': {'profileUsername': 'Gitcoin Media', 'imageHeight': 720, 'description': 'In our fireside this week, we\'ll be leading a discussion on Module 5, Tokens & Mechanism Design. We\'ll ask that you read it beforehand, interrupt us often, use the chat as a tool for thought (which was great last week). We’ll be expanding Q&A for more discussion. From this week\'s materials:   The word "token" shares a root with the Germanic and Dutch words for "teach", which makes sense given that tokens transmit factual information. This is the actual use of tokens, and mechanisms designed around them, in Web 3: they are tools that can be used to teach by creating tangible, verifiable incentives for certain behaviours, both individually and collectively.  We\'ll talk all about how these tokens and the facts they represent give us a chance to solve two major problems with the internet today: discoverability and moderation.  We\'ll let these ideas together with an exploration of Amazon in Unbounded Search and lessons from the best mechanism designers on the internet: game designers.   With these examples, we hope to paint the case that beyond the financial,  tokens can be used to build pro-social, valuable games which simultaneously solve major issues with the modern internet. Join us if you can -- and check out the materials when time permits :)', 'video': 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/NUO86413eD4', 'articleComments': '0', 'articleViews': '193', 'imageWidth': 1280, 'title': 'Tokens & Mechanism Design with Sparrow, Bea Ramos| KERNEL Fireside 2/18', 'imageSecureUrl': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NUO86413eD4/maxresdefault.jpg', 'articleLikes': '4', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NUO86413eD4', 'site_name': 'Tokens & Mechanism Design with Sparrow, Bea Ramos', 'favicon': 'https://www.youtube.com/favicon.ico', 'articleFavorites': '0', 'type': 'photo'}, 'modDate': '2022-08-14T12:35:41.669Z'}
