2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '0d3c5e73-8950-4028-8a04-01af92ce7416', '_id': 'Documents/0d3c5e73-8950-4028-8a04-01af92ce7416', '_rev': '_e41s5ym---', 'createDate': '2022-10-06T15:34:20.745Z', 'data': {'type': 'website', 'site_name': 'Belfer Center for Science and International Affairs', 'title': 'Bridging-Based Ranking', 'description': 'There is significant concern about the engagement-based ranking systems used by TikTok, Facebook, YouTube, etc. to recommend content. Bridging-based ranking systems can address one of the most dangerous aspects of such algorithmic\xa0recommendations—the push toward polarization and divisiveness that is tearing nations apart—and do so without reducing anonymity or increasing censorship. This report\xa0explores what bridging-based ranking is, how it helps (overcoming downsides of chronological feeds and middleware), addresses common objections, and provides early examples of its use and benefits in the wild. The report concludes by providing next steps for platforms, governments, funders, and researchers\xa0in order to accelerate the deployment of bridging.', 'image': 'https://www.belfercenter.org/sites/default/files/styles/shared_image/public/images/publication/feature/727ed7cf-fc16-4fef-9e5f-1dc6ff1ae228_social_media_by_picasso.png?h=4d969e4b&itok=voX6HX_H', 'url': 'https://www.belfercenter.org/publication/bridging-based-ranking', 'favicon': 'https://www.belfercenter.org/sites/default/files/favicon.ico'}, 'modDate': '2022-10-06T15:34:20.745Z'}
