2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '927050b4-2dfb-4159-bd86-5dd724d623a1', '_id': 'Documents/927050b4-2dfb-4159-bd86-5dd724d623a1', '_rev': '_e50M1aG--A', 'createDate': '2022-10-09T16:23:20.258Z', 'data': {'imageSecureUrl': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LcxOdWWL8xs/maxresdefault.jpg', 'articleLikes': '562', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LcxOdWWL8xs', 'site_name': 'Full Stack Web3 with Lens Protocol, Next.js, and GraphQL', 'favicon': 'https://www.youtube.com/favicon.ico', 'imageWidth': 1280, 'articleViews': '11846', 'articleComments': '65', 'type': 'photo', 'profileUsername': 'Nader Dabit', 'imageHeight': 720, 'description': 'In this video you\'ll learn how to use Lens Protocol to build out a basic social media application.  🔗 Lens Protocol Starter - https://github.com/dabit3/lens-protocol-frontend 🔗 Lens Protocol Subgraph - https://github.com/protofire/lens-protocol-subgraph 🔗 Example codebase from tutorial - https://github.com/dabit3/lens-youtube-tutorial 🔗 Lens Protocol Developer Docs - https://lens.xyz/garden  We\'ll create a new Next.js app, install our dependencies, then query for user profiles. We\'ll then update the UI to list profiles and their metadata, and allow users to click on a profile and navigate to an individual profile view to see the user\'s posts.  Next we\'ll add a follow button to initialize a transaction in the smart contract to enable "follow" functionality. By the end of the video you should have a good understanding of how to use Lens protocol to build out your own applications.  0:00 - Introduction 3:33 - Project initialization and installing dependencies 4:41 - Creating the first query 12:00 - Rendering profiles in the UI 19:55 - Creating the profile page 37:49 - Following a user 44:44 - Wrapping up', 'video': 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/LcxOdWWL8xs', 'articleFavorites': '0', 'title': 'Full Stack Web3 with Lens Protocol, Next.js, and GraphQL - Building a Social Media App'}, 'modDate': '2022-10-09T16:23:20.258Z'}
