2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '5bc9fc88-5915-4b15-a725-d12fb2387efa', '_id': 'Documents/5bc9fc88-5915-4b15-a725-d12fb2387efa', '_rev': '_gGzEk82--_', 'createDate': '2023-06-05T20:36:34.925Z', 'data': {'image': 'https://d31ygswzsyecnt.cloudfront.net/grants/ec40778ccc23ccb1623b16ee70aea8ff/Screen_Shot_2022-03-07_at_11.16.13_PM.png', 'site_name': 'impactdao.game | Grants', 'description': "The vision for the cartographers group is to support the impactDAOs ecosystem to use web3 to create massive positive change. We need a connective tissue, an ImpactDAO hub to where projects find each other, to connect how individual efforts unlock key pieces of the broader societal shift, to share high-value composable frameworks others can leverage to supercharge their impact.  But we need to first re-build the foundational layer that will truly shift the underlying levellers that prevent entrepreneurs, builders, and communities from pursuing truly impactful work. A focus on building Technologies for Humanity. Climate (and existential risks) is a problem that needs to be tackled not only by removing more carbon from the atmosphere or shifting to cleaner energy sources. We see climate issues as a result of economies driven by the extraction of resources, efficiency and speed rather than diversity and ecosystemic value. To solve this climate crisis, we need to re-engineer what drives our economies and how we coordinate as humans for which we need more communication across networks, share insights on each organization's learnings, more talent flowing to these solutions, be able to fork strategies, and experiment and iterate with web3 strategies to achieve large scale impact. Our initial efforts studied the work of 185 impactdaos using web3 to create positive externalities, identify best practices, enable synergies and host events to bring builders together. Now the focus lies on 1. Building the values-based economy 2. Coordination between impact collectives and, most importantly, accelerate the opportunities for those building foundational Technologies for Humanity.  Building a values-based economy. How can we use web3 to build an economy that inherently creates, captures and encourages real-world positive value. An economy that will prioritize impact over anything else. We can leverage programable money to build currencies backed by what we care about like natural assets. Yet, another first step might be forking capitalism for impact. A potential first step is to create Hypercertificates:  While the technical specs are in development, we’ve been on an exploration to identify the highest value-add market areas were to launch this and what are the ingredients of a successful initial marketplace. If this is successful, this will unlock start-up financing dynamics for public goods, an exit scenario for work that would otherwise have no way to capture value, a shift in how we value companies away from profits to focus on outcomes, increased funding for riskier endeavours, better capital allocation, outcomes-based financing, and more talent dedicating amazing skills to create public goods. In the long-term, this will shift incentive structures to support and reward work, creating positive externalities, and will encourage entrepreneurs to optimize for impact because that is what the market optimizes for. This new marketplace will be launched in Q1 2023  Accelerating Technologies for Humanity We need incredible people to bring about massive change. The absolute best entrepreneurs, shapers and creators are those who are uniquely obsessed with a problem and have a radically new way to bring this to the world. We are convinced that the best approach is to work with the builders who are obsessed with a particular problem, who can move masses and create visions to regenerate the world. Only after that, explore if there is any way web3 accelerates their chances of success.Technologies for Humanity in all its forms: innovation, machines, agriculture, knowledge, practices, community, money, web3, etc.  The humble beginnings will be new forms of community events to enable cross-sectional ideation, connections, etc. eg. Feedback sessions: show up, and you know you will be paired with 3 other high-quality folks to aim to solve each other’s challenges.  Next? is a cohort-based program for those working on impactful visions in deeptech, to explore how to approach entrepreneurship with a regenerative, future view on humanity. We will explore can web3 (the tech, financing or ethos) supercharge their mission, or maybe just the web3 ethos. Next? fellowships to support those with crazy impactful visions to dedicate their young years to learning intersectional wisdom and exploring new solutions to drive change. Next? community houses that focus on the technical but, most importantly, on the soft skills to grow internally and to grow insanely successful visions and ventures in a way that prioritises nature and society’s regeneration. Community events have already started, one-to-one support has too, now the aim is to scale the reach with more events and with a first inaugural cohort. The aim is to launch the first cohort in February 2023.  Coordination Cartographers bridge collaborations between impact verticals. From refi to desci, from public goods funding to impact evaluation, from open science publication to carbon markets. We coordinate the action across impact verticals. Another layer of coordination is the meta layer, this is were I’ve spent most of my recent time - connecting groups that coordinate and support individual work. Protocol Labs, PrimeDAO, Desci Labs, Molecule, Celo, SCRF, DAO Research Collective, Crowdmuse, Kernel, Gitcoin, and Protein, are all coordination collectives and going forward, it will be super important to have a shared sense of truth and clear ways to join and supercharge efforts.  What we have done since last grant round: Regular meetings with impact evaluators, builders, and entrepreneurs to organize around a collective approach. Continue to grow the impactDAOs list.  2 work-in-progress studies as a follow-up of the impactDAO research. These are particularly focused on 1. different funding mechanisms that we can use to support projects: from advanced market commitment to retroactive funding to tokens and credits. 2. use cases for adaptation and resilience solutions for climate change Since June, we have been working with the Networked Goods Funding at Protocol Labs and the RaidGuild team. We are developing the architecture to be able to mint, sell and burn impact certificates on-chain. Collaborations with other coordination groups to provide insight and build new primitives and collective projects lists, etc. Stewarded conferences, working groups around specific topics and smaller meetups for particular impact verticals. Funding the Commons, 2 Technologies for Humanity meetups, topic-specific group chats, and organizing Bogota events, etc.  This group has focused a lot of the work on making connections across ideas, industries, people and organizations. This entails connecting builders working on similar primitives, organizing events with intersectional speakers, funders with grantees and growing the ecosystem in a way that supports each other. This includes brainstorming with countless early projects on how to approach the use of web3, and advising in hackathons. Another example is co-creating research artefacts with web3 sceptical in industries like climate or health sciences to find points of synergies.  Focus on the background work to enable connections across ideas, industries, people and organizations. This entails connecting builders working on similar primitives, organizing events with intersectional speakers, funders with grantees and growing the ecosystem in a way that supports each other. This includes brainstorming with countless early projects on how to approach the use of web3, and advising in hackathons. Another example is co-creating research artefacts with web3 sceptical in industries like climate or health sciences to find points of synergies.  Contributed to multiple web3 hackathons to judge and advise projects on building regenerative work. Brought the impactDAO perspective to a range of conferences from ETHBarcelona to Future Forum to the DAO Research Stanford Workshop to the upcoming Foresight’s Crypto, AI and Security event.", 'title': 'impactdao.game | Grants', 'url': 'https://bounties.gitcoin.co/grants/5005/impact-cartographers-coalition', 'favicon': 'https://d31ygswzsyecnt.cloudfront.net/static/v2/images/favicon.ico/favicon-32x32.png', 'type': 'website'}, 'modDate': '2023-06-05T20:36:34.925Z'}
