2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '3d35a158-dce4-44a7-b729-91de94bfaf9c', '_id': 'Documents/3d35a158-dce4-44a7-b729-91de94bfaf9c', '_rev': '_grdxtdu--A', 'data': {'site_name': 'Summer School 2024', 'title': 'Corals, Carbon And The Cosmos: The Story Of Hyperbolic Space - Summer School 2024', 'articleSection': 'News', 'favicon': 'https://ss.amsi.org.au/wp-content/uploads/sites/100/2022/08/ss_favicon.png', 'url': 'https://ss.amsi.org.au/corals-carbon-and-the-cosmos-the-story-of-hyperbolic-space/', 'articlePublishedTime': '2016-02-18T07:08:11+00:00', 'locale': 'en_US', 'type': 'article', 'image': 'https://ss.amsi.org.au/wp-content/uploads/sites/100/2023/07/summerschool24.png', 'description': 'Throughout the natural world – in corals, cactuses, sea-slugs and lettuce leaves – we see swooping, curving and crenelated forms. All these are biological manifestations of hyperbolic geometry an alternative to the Euclidean geometry we learn about in school. While nature has been playing with permutations of hyperbolic space for hundreds of millions of years, …'}, 'modDate': '2023-09-27T18:43:09.948Z', 'createDate': '2023-09-27T18:43:09.948Z'}
