2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '15b7fd83-4da3-4632-9bda-9d1e8e9e10e8', '_id': 'Documents/15b7fd83-4da3-4632-9bda-9d1e8e9e10e8', '_rev': '_groogs6---', 'data': {'type': 'site', 'site_name': 'A response to\xa0The Economist', 'description': '“For what is Europe, if not a post-growth continent already?”, the author writes, before hailing Italy as a post-growth utopia. Classic mistake. In reality,\xa0degrowth differs fundamentally from a recession. A\xa0recession\xa0is a reduction in GDP, one that happens accidently, often with undesirable social outcomes like unemployment, austerity, and poverty. Degrowth, on the other hand, is a planned, selective and equitable downscaling of economic activities. Recession: unplanned and unwanted. Degrowth: designed and desired. Associating degrowth with a recession just because the two involve a reduction of GDP is absurd; it would be like arguing that an amputation and a diet are the very same thing just because they both lead to weight loss.', 'title': 'A response to\xa0The Economist: Shut up and let me grow\xa0\xa0\xa0 – Timothée Parrique', 'url': 'https://timotheeparrique.com/a-response-to-the-economist-shut-up-and-let-me-grow/'}, 'modDate': '2023-09-28T07:22:04.398Z', 'createDate': '2023-09-28T07:22:04.398Z'}
