2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '6591de22-d9e1-4492-b73c-b32ee6654ea3', '_id': 'Documents/6591de22-d9e1-4492-b73c-b32ee6654ea3', '_rev': '_hIEHM7a--A', 'data': {'imageHeight': '400', 'type': 'website', 'image': 'http://static.pocketcasts.com/discover/images/400/0d61e220-afd9-0139-c1a4-0acc26574db2.jpg', 'url': 'https://pca.st/13q1e5t1', 'favicon': 'https://pca.st/assets/favicon-196-b1900d68124e6536dbd72ef0c1558fab4518693a06e3a9e9a48254835a2d3473.png', 'title': '11/26/23 - Vanessa Machado de Oliveira Andreotti (Repeat) - First Voices Radio', 'imageWidth': '400', 'site_name': 'Pocket Casts', 'description': "This week we're revisiting Tiokasin Ghosthorse's conversation with Professor Vanessa Machado de Oliveira Andreotti, author of “Hospicing Modernity: Facing Humanity’s Wrongs and Implications for Social Activism” (North Atlantic Books, 2021). The original broadcast aired in March 2023. Vanessa is a Latinx professor at the University of British Columbia and holds a Canada Research Chair in Race, Inequalities and Global Change. Vanessa began her career as a teacher in Brazil in 1994 and has since led educational and research programs in countries including the UK, Finland, Aotearoa/New Zealand, Brazil and Canada. She works across sectors in international and comparative education, particularly focusing on global justice and citizenship, Indigenous and community engagement, sustainability, and social and ecological responsibility. Her research examines relationships between historical, systemic, and ongoing forms of violence, and the inherent unsustainability of modernity. Vanessa is one of the founding member", 'imageSecureUrl': 'https://static.pocketcasts.com/discover/images/400/0d61e220-afd9-0139-c1a4-0acc26574db2.jpg'}, 'modDate': '2023-12-25T15:12:54.743Z', 'createDate': '2023-12-25T15:12:54.743Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '582aca07-dc7d-4186-9308-d414ff62c592', '_id': 'Documents/582aca07-dc7d-4186-9308-d414ff62c592', '_rev': '_hJAwPGi--_', 'data': {'site_name': 'arXiv.org', 'description': 'Large Language Models (LLMs) have taken Knowledge Representation -- and the world -- by storm. This inflection point marks a shift from explicit knowledge representation to a renewed focus on the hybrid representation of both explicit knowledge and parametric knowledge. In this position paper, we will discuss some of the common debate points within the community on LLMs (parametric knowledge) and Knowledge Graphs (explicit knowledge) and speculate on opportunities and visions that the renewed focus brings, as well as related research topics and challenges.', 'imageSecureUrl': 'https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/arxiv-logo-fb.png', 'imageWidth': '1200', 'type': 'website', 'url': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.06374v1', 'title': 'Large Language Models and Knowledge Graphs: Opportunities and Challenges', 'imageHeight': '700', 'image': 'https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/arxiv-logo-fb.png', 'favicon': 'https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/favicon-32x32.png'}, 'modDate': '2023-12-28T13:52:02.184Z', 'createDate': '2023-12-28T13:52:02.184Z'}
