2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '627839e8-2aa5-4d72-adb7-04f2cb58752a', '_id': 'Documents/627839e8-2aa5-4d72-adb7-04f2cb58752a', '_rev': '_h8lKGGu--A', 'data': {'articlePublishedTime': 'Sat Jun 10 2023 02:27:22 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)', 'type': 'article', 'site_name': 'Beyond_*', 'url': 'https://beyond.pubpub.org/pub/egppkxes/release/1', 'title': 'Fractal Communalism — social experiments, anarchist futures in the present', 'description': 'US American communes are as old as the country itself. The earliest communes were for the most part religious in nature, while a more recent wave was the hippie communes of the mid twentieth century. The goals and impact of the communes has not always been consistent. However, on studying the communes as a distributed experimental ecosystem, a different perspective begins to emerge. Communes and intentional communities constitute experimental societies, where humans gather to explore new ways of making decisions, collective organizing and alternative forms of hierarchy. Famous examples of experimental communities include Oroville, Twin Oaks, Arcosanti, Damanhur all of which have shown us different ways of living and being. Here I describe both digital and analogue aspects of how these communities form "collectives of collectives,” which, beyond their individual spaces, comprise entire ecosystems of communal experiments that demonstrate diverse examples of humanity’s potentiality and sociality through deeply collaborative networks.', 'image': 'https://beyond.pubpub.org/static/logoWhite.svg'}, 'modDate': '2024-06-05T19:07:00.108Z', 'createDate': '2024-06-05T19:07:00.108Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '7cd8e8ce-7868-485e-bda1-cafd790fc843', '_id': 'Documents/7cd8e8ce-7868-485e-bda1-cafd790fc843', '_rev': '_h8lNjKm--A', 'data': {'type': 'article', 'image': 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/corehtml/pmc/pmcgifs/pmc-card-share.jpg?_=0', 'description': 'Cooperation is needed for evolution to construct new levels of organization. The emergence of genomes, cells, multi-cellular organisms, social insects and human society are all based on cooperation. Cooperation means that selfish replicators forgo some ...', 'site_name': 'PubMed Central (PMC)', 'title': 'Five rules for the evolution of cooperation', 'url': 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3279745/', 'favicon': 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/coreutils/nwds/img/favicons/favicon-192.png'}, 'modDate': '2024-06-05T19:10:46.474Z', 'createDate': '2024-06-05T19:10:46.474Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '8783d730-979f-4ab6-b47d-d8b2e21dc55e', '_id': 'Documents/8783d730-979f-4ab6-b47d-d8b2e21dc55e', '_rev': '_h8lT5ae--A', 'data': {'title': 'Cosmolocalism: Understanding the Transitional Dynamics Towards Post-Capitalism        | tripleC: Communication, Capitalism & Critique. Open Access Journal for a Global Sustainable Information Society', 'description': 'Over the last decades, the proliferation of ICTs and capitalist markets has created a new social-historical reality for communication, production and societal organisation, while social inequality has deepened. In this context, alternative forms of organisation based on the commons have emerged, challenging the core values of capitalism. Within this new form of egalitarian and transnational collaborative networks, a new concept of social coexistence has been proposed: cosmolocalism. This article presents the genealogy of cosmolocalism and compares it to previous conceptual universalist reconfigurations, namely cosmopolitanism and internationalism. While the current discourse on cosmolocalism focuses on production and distribution, its political dynamics and limitations remain unexplored. Our ultimate goal is to open a path of inquiry for further reflection and deliberation.', 'type': 'site', 'site_name': 'Cosmolocalism: Understanding the Transitional Dynamics Towards Post', 'image': 'https://www.triple-c.at/public/journals/1/pageHeaderLogoImage_en_US.png', 'url': 'https://www.triple-c.at/index.php/tripleC/article/view/1188'}, 'modDate': '2024-06-05T19:17:42.471Z', 'createDate': '2024-06-05T19:17:42.471Z'}
