2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': 'cf8ef737-e759-4bc3-8c80-6157c9c96fea', '_id': 'Documents/cf8ef737-e759-4bc3-8c80-6157c9c96fea', '_rev': '_iIvnKWu--A', 'data': {'description': 'Weird Economies (W.E), is a journal, programming space and social experimental site that traces economic imaginaries extraordinary to financial arrangements of our time. W.E takes on an expanded chrono-political strategy, wherein past (vindication), present (location), and future (fabrication) are commensurable grounds for the extrapolation of weird—and weirder—economies.', 'url': 'https://weirdeconomies.com', 'imageHeight': '720', 'image': 'https://weirdeconomies.com/assets/screenshot.jpg', 'imageType': 'image/jpg', 'imageWidth': '1280', 'site_name': 'Weird Economies', 'title': 'Weird Economies', 'type': 'website', 'favicon': 'https://weirdeconomies.com/assets/favicon-32x32.png'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-13T14:04:53.516Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-13T14:04:53.516Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': 'f9b019e9-b0a3-4af0-8f01-e072882801b2', '_id': 'Documents/f9b019e9-b0a3-4af0-8f01-e072882801b2', '_rev': '_iIvrg_---A', 'data': {'title': 'SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT INDEX', 'imageHeight': '664', 'site_name': 'SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT INDEX', 'type': 'website', 'imageWidth': '1250', 'favicon': 'https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5c77afeb7fdcb89805fab2a0/1575216090294-8WYTS5Q7454C6K58V083/favicon.ico', 'image': 'http://static1.squarespace.com/static/5c77afeb7fdcb89805fab2a0/t/668e54b072602b1b3bc87e47/1720603834913/Map.png?format=1500w', 'description': 'The Sustainable Development Index (SDI) measures the ecological efficiency of human development, recognizing that development must be achieved within planetary boundaries. It was created to update the Human Development Index (HDI) for the ecological realities of the Anthropocene.', 'url': 'https://www.sustainabledevelopmentindex.org'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-13T14:09:37.808Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-13T14:09:37.808Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '13115b39-e7e4-42dd-a77c-fecaad7f8f76', '_id': 'Documents/13115b39-e7e4-42dd-a77c-fecaad7f8f76', '_rev': '_iJXKdIa---', 'data': {'type': 'site', 'site_name': 'The prospect of wise public policy (AI – A Partner in Wise Democracy? #7) – Random Communications from an Evolutionary Edge', 'description': 'I had a conversation with Claude, one of my AI colleagues, which I share here. \xa0Starting with a prompt about wise public policy, we delved into the tension between the needs of people vs nature, which Claude addressed well, I thought, including notes about the root causes of that tension. We both agreed that actually addressing all that would be a fundamentally transformational challenge – in response to which Claude offered some overall guidance about “getting better at change itself”. \xa0I found it fascinating. The whole conversation took less than an hour, again with the vast majority of that time spent by me crafting my fairly complex prompts which Claude then had no problem rapidly and competently responding to… – Tom', 'title': 'The prospect of wise public policy (AI – A Partner in Wise Democracy? #7) – Random Communications from an Evolutionary Edge', 'url': 'https://www.tomatleeblog.com/archives/175328974'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-15T12:09:44.358Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-15T12:09:44.358Z'}
