2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '7656ede7-b16a-4452-b3df-5c8d99bca066', '_id': 'Documents/7656ede7-b16a-4452-b3df-5c8d99bca066', '_rev': '_iKculIi--A', 'data': {'imageType': 'image/jpeg', 'site_name': 'Metamoderna', 'articlePublishedTime': '2017-04-08T19:46:21+00:00', 'description': 'These people are not just annoying, they are also about to take over the world. They are the ones with the highest amount of cultural capital, which they trade at increasingly favorable exchange rates, and, with which they’ll eventually outcompete capitalism. And their progressive and postmaterialist values generally make them more concerned with the transition to an ecologically and socially sustainable society than making a buck to buy nice things. It’s not that they are better than normal folks, but they are the ones to invent all the things to save the world.', 'type': 'article', 'imageWidth': '1132', 'favicon': 'https://i0.wp.com/metamoderna.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/MM_faceprofil.png?fit=160%2C160&ssl=1', 'articleModifiedTime': '2020-04-27T21:53:21+00:00', 'image': 'https://metamoderna.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/HHH.jpg', 'title': 'The Reign of Hackers, Hipsters & Hippies - Metamoderna', 'imageHeight': '539', 'url': 'https://metamoderna.org/hackers-hipsters-hippies/', 'locale': 'en_US'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-18T21:12:38.825Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-18T21:12:38.825Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '12ff5122-4602-4cc5-8f0e-be4f8b2c3404', '_id': 'Documents/12ff5122-4602-4cc5-8f0e-be4f8b2c3404', '_rev': '_iL_N-p6--_', 'data': {'imageWidth': '1200', 'type': 'article', 'favicon': 'https://static.guim.co.uk/images/favicon-32x32.ico', 'articlePublishedTime': '2024-06-26T10:00:14.000Z', 'articleSection': 'Opinion', 'title': 'Silicon Valley wants unfettered control of the tech market. That’s why it’s cosying up to Trump | Evgeny Morozov', 'image': 'https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/7d07286cac9145e1a1a3ef34d63434571296baec/0_0_5400_3240/master/5400.jpg?width=1200&height=630&quality=85&auto=format&fit=crop&overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&overlay-width=100p&overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctb3BpbmlvbnMucG5n&enable=upscale&s=9545516fdc23da2e8afa9bb209038fce', 'articleModifiedTime': '2024-06-26T10:02:08.000Z', 'articleAuthor': 'https://www.theguardian.com/profile/evgeny-morozov', 'site_name': 'the Guardian', 'description': 'Spooked by Biden’s wealth tax, big tech venture capitalists are showing their progressive credentials were only ever skin deep, says writer Evgeny Morozov', 'url': 'https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/26/silicon-valley-tech-market-donald-trump-joe-biden-wealth-tax-big-tech-venture-capitalists', 'imageHeight': '720'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-20T13:22:37.374Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-20T13:22:37.374Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '2328e025-3324-46ab-b8d7-2810ceb1cfa8', '_id': 'Documents/2328e025-3324-46ab-b8d7-2810ceb1cfa8', '_rev': '_iLAOiXK--A', 'data': {'articleLikes': '650', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vVqPRah5hAY', 'favicon': 'https://www.youtube.com/favicon.ico', 'imageSecureUrl': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vVqPRah5hAY/maxresdefault.jpg', 'video': 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/vVqPRah5hAY', 'profileUsername': 'Nate Hagens', 'imageWidth': 1280, 'articleFavorites': '0', 'title': 'The Reality Party | Frankly #66', 'type': 'photo', 'imageHeight': 720, 'articleComments': '175', 'description': 'Recorded July 16 2024  Description  Following the attempted assassination of former United States President Donald J. Trump, Nate reflects on the dysfunctional social dynamics which have brought many of us to high levels of tribalism and mistrust toward others and divorced from the deeper challenges facing us in coming decades.  As humans, we all - for the most part - share the same enjoyments in life - beautiful nature, autonomy, music, healthy, tasty food, clean water, friends, and family (whatever species they might come in). Values are rarely - if ever - right or wrong, but they can become a polarizing force if they are blindly pursued without the broader context of the carbon pulse and what brought us here.  Is it even possible to have a political platform underpinned by a shared understanding that we live as part of the web of life, recognizing the centrality of energy and ecosystems, and seeing the limits of technology?  Could we align our political choices with these realities and be more effective, open to others, and act in a bi-partisan manner as citizens of the world?    For Show Notes and More: https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/frankly-original/66-reality-party  00:00 Introduction and Context 01:48 Shared Human Preferences 04:00 Core Values and Political Divides 05:47 Observations on Current Reality 07:12 Energy and Sustainability Issues 09:51 Human Nature and Environmental Impact 12:26 Technology and the Human Predicament 13:36 Conclusion and Call for Dialogue', 'site_name': 'The Reality Party', 'articleViews': '8823'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-20T14:34:13.778Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-20T14:34:13.778Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '939cc618-5023-4d02-9327-00dab288f4bf', '_id': 'Documents/939cc618-5023-4d02-9327-00dab288f4bf', '_rev': '_iLPdtMG--A', 'data': {'imageHeight': '700', 'imageWidth': '1200', 'imageSecureUrl': 'https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/arxiv-logo-fb.png', 'type': 'website', 'image': 'https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/arxiv-logo-fb.png', 'favicon': 'https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/favicon-32x32.png', 'title': 'AI Agents That Matter', 'description': 'AI agents are an exciting new research direction, and agent development is driven by benchmarks. Our analysis of current agent benchmarks and evaluation practices reveals several shortcomings that hinder their usefulness in real-world applications. First, there is a narrow focus on accuracy without attention to other metrics. As a result, SOTA agents are needlessly complex and costly, and the community has reached mistaken conclusions about the sources of accuracy gains. Our focus on cost in addition to accuracy motivates the new goal of jointly optimizing the two metrics. We design and implement one such optimization, showing its potential to greatly reduce cost while maintaining accuracy. Second, the benchmarking needs of model and downstream developers have been conflated, making it hard to identify which agent would be best suited for a particular application. Third, many agent benchmarks have inadequate holdout sets, and sometimes none at all. This has led to agents that are fragile because they take shortcuts and overfit to the benchmark in various ways. We prescribe a principled framework for avoiding overfitting. Finally, there is a lack of standardization in evaluation practices, leading to a pervasive lack of reproducibility. We hope that the steps we introduce for addressing these shortcomings will spur the development of agents that are useful in the real world and not just accurate on benchmarks.', 'site_name': 'arXiv.org', 'url': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.01502v1'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-21T08:19:22.466Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-21T08:19:22.466Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': 'eac04086-3edd-4cb1-bccd-88335d9c604c', '_id': 'Documents/eac04086-3edd-4cb1-bccd-88335d9c604c', '_rev': '_iLVw8Fa--_', 'data': {'imageHeight': '628', 'description': 'GARN is a network of organizations and individuals committed to the implementation of legal systems that respect and enforce Rights of Nature.', 'locale': 'en_US', 'image': 'https://www.garn.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Untitled-design.png', 'articlePublishedTime': '2020-10-12T14:05:53-05:00', 'imageSecureUrl': 'https://www.garn.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Untitled-design.png', 'imageWidth': '1200', 'title': 'Global Alliance for the Rights of Nature (GARN)', 'url': 'https://www.garn.org/', 'favicon': 'https://www.garn.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/GARN-logo-11.21.47.png', 'type': 'website', 'site_name': 'Global Alliance for the Rights of Nature (GARN)', 'imageType': 'image/png', 'articleModifiedTime': '2023-11-06T10:18:43-05:00'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-21T15:39:48.726Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-21T15:39:48.726Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '4431533a-edaf-47df-93d0-875f2cc65d07', '_id': 'Documents/4431533a-edaf-47df-93d0-875f2cc65d07', '_rev': '_iLWKN2O--A', 'data': {'type': 'site', 'site_name': 'LandPKS', 'favicon': 'https://landpotential.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/cropped-favicon-192x192.png', 'title': 'LandPKS | LandPKS', 'image': 'https://landpotential.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/cropped-favicon-180x180.png', 'description': 'Use the free LandPKS mobile app to discover the potential of your land and monitor change over time. Use your mobile device for soil identification, land cover and soil health monitoring, land management and farm record keeping, and more.', 'url': 'https://landpotential.org/'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-21T16:07:25.316Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-21T16:07:25.316Z'}
2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '68101551-62bd-4703-a666-1ba2af3d0802', '_id': 'Documents/68101551-62bd-4703-a666-1ba2af3d0802', '_rev': '_iLYsSZO---', 'data': {'image': 'http://www.rheingold.com/art/splitbrains/mac.gif', 'title': "howard rheingold's | tools for thought", 'description': 'Harry Truman was President and Sputnik was a word that only Russian language experts     knew when Doug Engelbart first thought about displaying words and images on radar screens, storing them in computers, and manipulating them with     levers and buttons and keyboards. For over thirty years, Engelbart has been trying to hasten what he believes will be the biggest step in     cultural evolution since the invention of the printing press. To hear him tell it today, both the computer establishment and the computer     revolutionaries still fail to understand that the art and power of using a computer as a mind amplifier are not in how the amplifier works but in     what the amplified minds are able to accomplish.', 'url': 'http://www.rheingold.com/texts/tft/09.html#Chap09', 'site_name': "howard rheingold's", 'type': 'site'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-21T19:04:26.803Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-21T19:04:26.803Z'}
