2025-04-09 11:10:44 - scrape_sites - WARNING - Missing URL in link: {'_key': '065f66d3-689e-4b65-940a-01f203f6952c', '_id': 'Documents/065f66d3-689e-4b65-940a-01f203f6952c', '_rev': '_iNC2m9m--A', 'data': {'favicon': 'https://www.youtube.com/favicon.ico', 'title': 'Audrey Tang: Homeschooler, 1st digital minister 🇹🇼 & 1st 🏳️\u200d⚧️ minister in 🌐 CoFounder Plurality.net', 'articleFavorites': '0', 'profileUsername': 'Modulo', 'imageWidth': 1280, 'site_name': 'Audrey Tang', 'type': 'photo', 'articleLikes': '11', 'imageSecureUrl': 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yC7_2AsUbww/maxresdefault.jpg', 'articleViews': '189', 'articleComments': '2', 'imageHeight': 720, 'video': 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/yC7_2AsUbww', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yC7_2AsUbww', 'description': 'In this episode, Manisha Snoyer hosts an illuminating heart-to-heart with Audrey Tang, Taiwan\'s first Minister of Digital Affairs, the co-creator of plurality.net and co-author of "Plurality: The Future of Collaborative Technology and Democracy." Audrey shares her visionary perspective on the role of technology in enhancing democratic systems, drawing from her rich background as a civic hacker and a homeschooler. They explore her journey from a child with a passion for computing to her profound insights on education and non-binary thinking. Audrey\'s reflections on her father\'s Socratic teaching methods and her mother\'s passion for Oregon-Oxford Debate, the cooperative schooling environment fostered by her parents, and her personal struggles and triumphs reveal how these experiences have shaped her understanding of true joyful learning and the potential of technology to create a more equitable and truly democratic society.  To join the Plurality Movement and read the book, go to : https://www.plurality.net/  For full show notes and all resources listed, visit: https://teachyourkids.substack.com/p/interview-with-audrey-tang-homeschooler'}, 'modDate': '2024-07-26T22:45:39.449Z', 'createDate': '2024-07-26T22:45:39.449Z'}
